        "explanationEn": "The correct Sanskrit word is «शुभः».\nFull Verse:\nस्वामिनारायणो मन्त्रो दिव्यश्चाऽलौकिकः शुभः।\nजप्योऽयं सकलैर्भक्तैर्दत्तोऽयं हरिणा स्वयम्॥ १०९॥\nMeaning: The ‘Swaminarayan’ mantra is divine, beyond this world and auspicious. Shri Hari himself bestowed this mantra. All devotees should chant it. In this mantra, understand that ‘Swami’ refers to Aksharbrahman, and ‘Narayan’ refers to Purushottam, who is superior to Aksharbrahman. (109–110)",
