        "explanationEn": "The correct Sanskrit word is «अङ्गं».\nFull Verse:\nपरस्माद् ब्रह्मणोऽन्यस्मिन्नक्षराद् ब्रह्मणस्तथा।\nप्रीत्यभावो हि वैराग्यम् अङ्गं भक्तेः सहायकम्॥ १२०॥\nMeaning: Vairāgya is to not have love for anything or anyone other than Parabrahman and Aksharbrahman. It serves to support bhakti. (120)",
