        "explanationEn": "The correct meaning of «ऊर्ध्वहस्तः» is «with arms raised».\nShloka 67: Thereafter, with mahimā and a steady mind, one should perform mālā while chanting the Swaminarayan mantra and having darshan of the murtis . Afterwards, while continuing to do darshan of the murtis , one should stand on one leg with arms raised and perform tapni mālā . (66–67)"
